Third-party components
----------------------

None. Stethoscope has no third-party dependency and no CDN.

Vendored from this project's own kits (same licence, same author), copied verbatim on 26/11/2026:

- web-kit 0.1.0 — docs/play/web-kit.js — the offline shell, storage helpers and PWA registration
- export-kit 1.0.0 — docs/play/export-kit.js — Blob download, used for the recording export

Neither kit is modified. Neither makes a network request.

Not a medical device
---------------------

This app records and compares the sound of a MACHINE — a fan, a pump, a grinder — against its own baseline.
It is not a medical device, it is not a stethoscope in the clinical sense, and it does not diagnose
anything. A low score means "this sounds different from how it sounded before", nothing more.

The analysis is a small DFT over a 256-sample window folded into eight bands, and a band-by-band comparison
against the baseline. A peak at a named frequency is a peak in that spectrum, not a claim about what is
wrong with the machine.

No microphone
-------------

There is no `getUserMedia`, no `MediaRecorder` and no `AudioContext` in this app: it works on a sample buffer
the page can hold and a test can check. A microphone would be a second job, and a privacy question the spec
does not ask for.
